---
name: std-fs-failure-raises
description: "std.fs raises on a missing path and on the wrong type — on the three lanes that agree; jvm is EXCLUDED and that is the finding"
backends: [int, js, v2, jvm]
---

# `std.fs` raises — and `backends:` above is the assertion

`specs/std-fs-os.md` §2.1. Every read-shaped `std.fs` operation raises on a missing path on
**int**, **js** and **v2-native**. `jvm` was missing from `backends:` until 2026-08-07,
and the exclusion was measured rather than cautious: with `jvm` added it failed on **exactly two
rows** —

    line 3: expected=listDir(missing)=raised  got=listDir(missing)=NO-RAISE(List())
    line 4: expected=listDir(file)=raised     got=listDir(file)=NO-RAISE(List())

— and every other row passed there. So the jvm divergence was `listDir` and nothing else:
`readFile`, `readBytes`, `copyFile` and `moveFile` already raised on jvm exactly as elsewhere. That
narrowing is what made the fix a two-line change to one runtime helper, filed and closed as
`jvm-listdir-answers-empty-where-every-other-lane-raises`. **The `jvm` on the line above IS that
closure** — the lane now calls `Files.list`, which this project's own spec always said it called,
and raises the same `NoSuchFileException` / `NotDirectoryException` the int lane raises.

⚠ Note for whoever reads a green run here: the corpus contract's canonical lanes are
`{int, js, v2}`, so the `jvm` entry above is exercised by `scripts/conformance` and NOT by the
nightly.

**Only the FACT of the raise is asserted, not its text**, because the text differs on every lane and
is not a contract: `NoSuchFileException` on int and jvm, `ENOENT` on js, a bare
`RuntimeException(path)` on native. That last one is its own problem — native erases the exception
TYPE, so `listDir` on a file and `listDir` on a missing path are indistinguishable there even
inside a `catch`. This case cannot see that; §2.1 records it.

Reported by **nadia** as `std-fs-failure-contract` (2026-08-04), whose first ask was that this
behaviour be stated at all.

```scalascript
[readFile, listDir, readBytes, copyFile, moveFile, mkdirs, writeFile](std/fs.ssc)

val root = "/tmp/ssc-fs-raises-case"
val dir  = root + "/adir"
val file = root + "/afile.txt"
val gone = root + "/does-not-exist"

mkdirs(dir)
writeFile(file, "x\n")

def raises(label: String, thunk: () => String): Unit =
  try
    val v = thunk()
    println(label + "=NO-RAISE(" + v + ")")
  catch
    case e: Throwable => println(label + "=raised")

raises("readFile(missing)", () => readFile(gone))
raises("readFile(dir)", () => readFile(dir))
raises("listDir(missing)", () => listDir(gone).toString)
raises("listDir(file)", () => listDir(file).toString)
raises("readBytes(missing)", () => readBytes(gone).length.toString)
raises("copyFile(missing)", () => { copyFile(gone, root + "/c1"); "ok" })
raises("moveFile(missing)", () => { moveFile(gone, root + "/m1"); "ok" })
```
